<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>O lovely Bridegroom, our nat’ral strength e’er fails us;</l><l>Hopeless Thou found us, and one gift Thou gave:</l><l>Our little pow’r to cling to our Beloved,</l><l>Leaning on Thee and guided all the way.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>O lovely Bridegroom, have mercy on Thy people</l><l>That we’d forsake all other loves but Thee,</l><l>Cleaving to Thee, our dear and faithful Husband;</l><l>Loving Thee solely, unreservedly.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>O lovely Bridegroom, Thy burning love compels us</l><l>That we’d be ready for that wedding day.</l><l>E’er we’d adorn the church with all Thy riches;</l><l>Her beauty then Thou wouldst desire for aye.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>O lovely Bridegroom, we yearn to hear Thy speaking:</l><l>“You’re altogether beautiful, My love!”</l><l>Aching for Thee, Thy coming we would hasten</l><l>Till at Thy wedding feast we meet above.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
